  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 222 AM EDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nHigh pressure moving across the Great Lakes region will keep us dry \nand cooler Monday, but then it will shift eastward as we go to \nmidweek. An upper ridge over the Central U.S. also will shift \neastward. The combination of higher thicknesses and southerly winds \nwill bring a return to above normal temperatures for Tue/Wed. \n\nThe upper ridge does look to flatten out Wed/Thu, as another cool \nfront drops into the Midwest. Passage looks to be in the Wed. \nnight/Thursday time frame. Troughing aloft may bring yet another \ncool front Friday night/Saturday.",
